(485552, 46670, 13064, '<td valign="top">The primary focus is lost in the background in parts.  like the general composition, althought he rock is taking a lot of focus to the bottom of the frame.</td>', 'The primary focus is lost in the background in parts.  like the general composition, althought he rock is taking a lot of focus to the bottom of the frame.', '2003-11-14 15:39:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(485554, 46527, 6999, '<td valign="top">Lots of good things - placement of light, impression of steel, and real roughness of texture in the background paper(?). Unconvinced by the processing, unconvinced by the conposition - the angling of it all seems arbitrary to me, and the mangling of pixels likewise - don;t see what you gain. Some sense of viciousness? Sharpness would better be expressed in a cleaner shot i think, and the loop of the handle being out of shot annoys me.</td>', 'Lots of good things - placement of light, impression of steel, and real roughness of texture in the background paper(?). Unconvinced by the processing, unconvinced by the conposition - the angling of it all seems arbitrary to me, and the mangling of pixels likewise - don;t see what you gain. Some sense of viciousness? Sharpness would better be expressed in a cleaner shot i think, and the loop of the handle being out of shot annoys me.', '2003-11-14 15:41:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(485556, 46410, 13064, '<td valign="top">I love this!!!  The contrast and the different textures are sensational.  Had to come back and comment on it. 10</td>', 'I love this!!!  The contrast and the different textures are sensational.  Had to come back and comment on it. 10', '2003-11-14 15:41:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(485559, 46668, 13064, '<td valign="top">Shiney stuff always works for me.  The highlights in the top of the heart curves are a little disconcerting. I like the graduated backround.<br/> <br/>The warmth of the wood and the red heart infill contrast wonderfully with the hardness of the metal. 8</td>', 'Shiney stuff always works for me.  The highlights in the top of the heart curves are a little disconcerting. I like the graduated backround. The warmth of the wood and the red heart infill contrast wonderfully with the hardness of the metal. 8', '2003-11-14 15:44:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(485561, 46483, 6999, '<td valign="top">Now if you''d called it The Manhattan Project, this would have been a scary photo. Neat trick of light though, and intriguing image. My eye is drawn to the blank foreground space though, and i don''t find anything of interst there - the tents and rubble seem too high in the frame to gain emphasis, but not insignificant enough to be ignored.Would love to see it cropped an inch or so from the bottom, not least to get the horizon out of the middle of the frame, which really doesn''t seem to suit this shot.</td>', 'Now if you''d called it The Manhattan Project, this would have been a scary photo. Neat trick of light though, and intriguing image. My eye is drawn to the blank foreground space though, and i don''t find anything of interst there - the tents and rubble seem too high in the frame to gain emphasis, but not insignificant enough to be ignored.Would love to see it cropped an inch or so from the bottom, not least to get the horizon out of the middle of the frame, which really doesn''t seem to suit this shot.', '2003-11-14 15:44:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(485562, 46229, 13064, '<td valign="top">I don''t know why but I really like this.  it almost seems like a point and shoot(but I doubt it), but everything fits and the movement in the imagery is great.</td>', 'I don''t know why but I really like this.  it almost seems like a point and shoot(but I doubt it), but everything fits and the movement in the imagery is great.', '2003-11-14 15:46:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(485563, 46320, 1280, '<td valign="top">Beautiful! I was going to do Peterson''s or Audubon guide, but couldn''t get it together in time.  Yours is good with good detail.  Especially the eye. Good dof too. 10!</td>', 'Beautiful! I was going to do Peterson''s or Audubon guide, but couldn''t get it together in time.  Yours is good with good detail.  Especially the eye. Good dof too. 10!', '2003-11-14 15:48:52.000000', NULL, 1),
