(486392, 45995, 3032, '<td valign="top">Really nice profile. I like it how the background transcends from dark to light and how the foreground, aided by the bird, follows that. <br/>The bird stands out nicely, especially because of the lighter edges.<br/>The piece of wood, with the lighter part helps to lead the eye into the frame. Funny to see those dead beatles lying there with their paws up. :)<br/> <br/>I do think that this pic is slightly oversharpened, the edge transitions are pretty harsh and the profile of the bird shows some pixelated step transitions. This has also led to some halos here and there.<br/> <br/>Overall a  good image. Good luck.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Really nice profile. I like it how the background transcends from dark to light and how the foreground, aided by the bird, follows that. The bird stands out nicely, especially because of the lighter edges.The piece of wood, with the lighter part helps to lead the eye into the frame. Funny to see those dead beatles lying there with their paws up. :) I do think that this pic is slightly oversharpened, the edge transitions are pretty harsh and the profile of the bird shows some pixelated step transitions. This has also led to some halos here and there. Overall a  good image. Good luck. ', '2003-11-15 17:22:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(486394, 46551, 3032, '<td valign="top">I liked this image from the first moment my eyes caught a glimpse of it. I think this is because of three reasons:<br/>1) Wonderful fall colors, light &amp; well composed (reflections)<br/>2) Peaceful landscape. It looks like a nice place to ponder about life, the universe and the rest. It is like: Stop! Take a rest........ Ahhhhhhh........... Ok, hit me with another week of work.<br/>3) Great use of leading lines. You''ve got the slope of the hill, the shoreline of the pond and the lines of the paths. The eye wanders across the frame.<br/> <br/>What really adds to this photo are the boats in front. Without them it would look too empty.<br/> <br/>The only thing I don''t like is the sky. Too white. But with the current rules you have to make a tradeoff between the sky or the foreground. It think you made the right choice.  9</td>', 'I liked this image from the first moment my eyes caught a glimpse of it. I think this is because of three reasons:1) Wonderful fall colors, light & well composed (reflections)2) Peaceful landscape. It looks like a nice place to ponder about life, the universe and the rest. It is like: Stop! Take a rest........ Ahhhhhhh........... Ok, hit me with another week of work.3) Great use of leading lines. You''ve got the slope of the hill, the shoreline of the pond and the lines of the paths. The eye wanders across the frame. What really adds to this photo are the boats in front. Without them it would look too empty. The only thing I don''t like is the sky. Too white. But with the current rules you have to make a tradeoff between the sky or the foreground. It think you made the right choice.  9', '2003-11-15 17:31:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(486398, 46631, 3032, '<td valign="top">Wonderful photo. The transition from highlights to shadow detail is just right. You see enough to form a picture of the scene, yet the main focus retains on the subject: milk in your coffee.<br/> <br/>I like the lighting, the colors, the toning and composition.<br/>The bubbles finish it off.<br/> <br/>9</td>', 'Wonderful photo. The transition from highlights to shadow detail is just right. You see enough to form a picture of the scene, yet the main focus retains on the subject: milk in your coffee. I like the lighting, the colors, the toning and composition.The bubbles finish it off. 9', '2003-11-15 17:34:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(486400, 46050, 3032, '<td valign="top">Good work.<br/>The mild misty toning, the well placed light effects, the facial expression, the color and the nudity seems to communicate the late sixties / early seventies from the 20th century.</td>', 'Good work.The mild misty toning, the well placed light effects, the facial expression, the color and the nudity seems to communicate the late sixties / early seventies from the 20th century.', '2003-11-15 17:38:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(486401, 46204, 3032, '<td valign="top">Wow, long exposure and moonlight? Awesome.<br/>I like it how the slope of the hill leads the eye trought the frame, suddenly you struck a ruin and the imagination comes up with its own fairytale.<br/> <br/>Wonderful exposure, colors and composition.</td>', 'Wow, long exposure and moonlight? Awesome.I like it how the slope of the hill leads the eye trought the frame, suddenly you struck a ruin and the imagination comes up with its own fairytale. Wonderful exposure, colors and composition.', '2003-11-15 17:40:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(486403, 46167, 3032, '<td valign="top">Well lit, excellent compositon. Good gray toning. Hard black/white border keeps the eye in the frame.<br/>The choice of aperture keeps the focus on the fingers. Perpaps that is one of the main elements in human bondage; focus on the person, not the rope. :)<br/> <br/>The long nail on the fifth finger leaves me wondering, are these the hands of a male or a female?</td>', 'Well lit, excellent compositon. Good gray toning. Hard black/white border keeps the eye in the frame.The choice of aperture keeps the focus on the fingers. Perpaps that is one of the main elements in human bondage; focus on the person, not the rope. :) The long nail on the fifth finger leaves me wondering, are these the hands of a male or a female?', '2003-11-15 17:46:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(486405, 46302, 3032, '<td valign="top">Nice seascape. I really like this composition with the shoreline in front, one cliff on the right,  another on the right and in an opposite angle the clouds.<br/>The lines work well here, the right cliff draws you down, the shoreline to the left edge, the right clif back into the centre and the clouds up up and away. :)<br/> <br/>Good job on the toning.</td>', 'Nice seascape. I really like this composition with the shoreline in front, one cliff on the right,  another on the right and in an opposite angle the clouds.The lines work well here, the right cliff draws you down, the shoreline to the left edge, the right clif back into the centre and the clouds up up and away. :) Good job on the toning.', '2003-11-15 17:50:12.000000', NULL, 1),
