(486785, 46422, 5225, '<td valign="top">Interesting Picture.</td>', 'Interesting Picture.', '2003-11-16 07:13:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(486789, 46614, 6999, '<td valign="top">Forbidden Colours huh? I work regularly with Ryuichi, not a song one sees a lot of around these days ...<br/> <br/>Quite a cool photo - though I''m not sure it holds the interest very long. Detail, focus, all that is fine - just think it''s a bit straightforward, and there isn''t the profoundly good lighting to turn that into something fascinating. 6</td>', 'Forbidden Colours huh? I work regularly with Ryuichi, not a song one sees a lot of around these days ... Quite a cool photo - though I''m not sure it holds the interest very long. Detail, focus, all that is fine - just think it''s a bit straightforward, and there isn''t the profoundly good lighting to turn that into something fascinating. 6', '2003-11-16 07:14:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(486790, 46357, 6999, '<td valign="top">I presume that reflection of a patch of light is the subject here. At first I thought it might echo one of the shapes in that slightly out of focus graphic, but it doesn''t - only perhaps the lower curve of it, and I can''t say I find anything particularly interesting in that. 1</td>', 'I presume that reflection of a patch of light is the subject here. At first I thought it might echo one of the shapes in that slightly out of focus graphic, but it doesn''t - only perhaps the lower curve of it, and I can''t say I find anything particularly interesting in that. 1', '2003-11-16 07:18:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(486793, 46097, 6999, '<td valign="top">have to presume this comesw from a very low res camera, else the pixelation is the result of some very bizarre processing. Not sure it would hold much interst even if perfectly reproduced here.</td>', 'have to presume this comesw from a very low res camera, else the pixelation is the result of some very bizarre processing. Not sure it would hold much interst even if perfectly reproduced here.', '2003-11-16 07:20:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(486800, 45693, 6999, '<td valign="top">Would love to see this with an even longer exposure - you''d probably need major ND filters to get that slow though - but the curves of the moving traffic would emphasise even more the yellow box at the junction. Intersting shot.</td>', 'Would love to see this with an even longer exposure - you''d probably need major ND filters to get that slow though - but the curves of the moving traffic would emphasise even more the yellow box at the junction. Intersting shot.', '2003-11-16 07:33:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(486802, 46088, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''m wonddering why you''ve shot it from this very ordinary angle, and whether a lower POV would help (my feeling: yes, enormously). Somewhat clutterd composition too, though I do like the attack hippo.</td>', 'I''m wonddering why you''ve shot it from this very ordinary angle, and whether a lower POV would help (my feeling: yes, enormously). Somewhat clutterd composition too, though I do like the attack hippo.', '2003-11-16 07:35:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(486804, 46551, 6999, '<td valign="top">Jeesh, Charon has a spare boat? Beautiful shot - like the near graphic quality given by the very still water and that tongue of land. Can''t quite imagine the borders of hell looking so peaceful, however :-)</td>', 'Jeesh, Charon has a spare boat? Beautiful shot - like the near graphic quality given by the very still water and that tongue of land. Can''t quite imagine the borders of hell looking so peaceful, however :-)', '2003-11-16 07:37:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(486808, 46419, 6999, '<td valign="top">Thoughtfully presented, and intriguing use of DOF to blur wat one would expect to be the real strength of this shot. I like the way it moves from a believable world - the texture of the in focus glass/metal - to the purely abstract over on the left; and the colours are good. The detail of that hook pulls far too much attention I think - oh, it''s the edge of the filament, isn''t it? - not convinced it should only have been partially shown, not sure what that achieves.</td>', 'Thoughtfully presented, and intriguing use of DOF to blur wat one would expect to be the real strength of this shot. I like the way it moves from a believable world - the texture of the in focus glass/metal - to the purely abstract over on the left; and the colours are good. The detail of that hook pulls far too much attention I think - oh, it''s the edge of the filament, isn''t it? - not convinced it should only have been partially shown, not sure what that achieves.', '2003-11-16 07:42:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(486821, 46563, 6668, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot but this thick black border does nothing for it in my opinion.</td>', 'Beautiful shot but this thick black border does nothing for it in my opinion.', '2003-11-16 08:39:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(486822, 46025, 6668, '<td valign="top">would be better without the actual book in the photo in my opinion.</td>', 'would be better without the actual book in the photo in my opinion.', '2003-11-16 08:42:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(486823, 46396, 6668, '<td valign="top">Absolutely beautiful, perfect lighting and composition, I give this a ten, hope to see it in the top 3!</td>', 'Absolutely beautiful, perfect lighting and composition, I give this a ten, hope to see it in the top 3!', '2003-11-16 08:46:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(486824, 45819, 6668, '<td valign="top">I don''t care much for the tight crop on this one, think it would have been better to show a little more of the car and maybe somemore space around it, it just feels to tight if that makes sense.</td>', 'I don''t care much for the tight crop on this one, think it would have been better to show a little more of the car and maybe somemore space around it, it just feels to tight if that makes sense.', '2003-11-16 08:48:24.000000', NULL, 1),
