(488026, 46622, 11895, '<td valign="top">I like that the needle is in sharp focus but wonder what color would have been like</td>', 'I like that the needle is in sharp focus but wonder what color would have been like', '2003-11-17 11:18:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(488049, 46564, 12327, '<td valign="top">Nice depth of field in this photo.  I would have cropped out the part where the needle starts to curve... maybe it''s just me, but it distracts me because my brain expects to see a straight needle, and then this one curves all of the sudden.  8</td>', 'Nice depth of field in this photo.  I would have cropped out the part where the needle starts to curve... maybe it''s just me, but it distracts me because my brain expects to see a straight needle, and then this one curves all of the sudden.  8', '2003-11-17 11:59:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(488060, 46676, 10643, '<td valign="top">softer lighting (not the flash) would make this much less stark and more welcoming. diffused lighting avoids such harsh shadows and the blown-out highlights like on the metal pan. the emotion and fun of the picture come through but the flash detracts. would also like a little more attention to wardrobe; a simple shirt without the "san francisco" would have been better.</td>', 'softer lighting (not the flash) would make this much less stark and more welcoming. diffused lighting avoids such harsh shadows and the blown-out highlights like on the metal pan. the emotion and fun of the picture come through but the flash detracts. would also like a little more attention to wardrobe; a simple shirt without the "san francisco" would have been better.', '2003-11-17 12:17:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(488061, 46369, 11895, '<td valign="top">more depth of Field would have appealed to me more</td>', 'more depth of Field would have appealed to me more', '2003-11-17 12:18:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(488063, 46638, 10643, '<td valign="top">a literal interpretation would be a large shotglass, preferably full. this looks like a regular size shotglass. I''m also not sure wha the thing on the left is, and I don''t think black and white is a good choice with props like deeply colored whiskey and a rose.</td>', 'a literal interpretation would be a large shotglass, preferably full. this looks like a regular size shotglass. I''m also not sure wha the thing on the left is, and I don''t think black and white is a good choice with props like deeply colored whiskey and a rose.', '2003-11-17 12:18:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(488078, 46452, 10643, '<td valign="top">the book title is "the," not "this," and I don''t see how this relates. is motorcycle racing small stuff?</td>', 'the book title is "the," not "this," and I don''t see how this relates. is motorcycle racing small stuff?', '2003-11-17 12:32:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(488079, 45828, 12325, '<td valign="top">I think this is a really good idea, carried off nicely ... but perhaps a more artistic interpretation could have been more striking?  For instance, I feel that the ceiling and the light detract from the picture.  If this could have been taken someplace with a uniform background, I would probably be even more impressed.  I''m envisioning it maybe a solid black with only the faces illuminated?  (just an example).  As it is, it comes across kind of "snapshot"-y.</td>', 'I think this is a really good idea, carried off nicely ... but perhaps a more artistic interpretation could have been more striking?  For instance, I feel that the ceiling and the light detract from the picture.  If this could have been taken someplace with a uniform background, I would probably be even more impressed.  I''m envisioning it maybe a solid black with only the faces illuminated?  (just an example).  As it is, it comes across kind of "snapshot"-y.', '2003-11-17 12:32:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(488086, 46128, 13648, '<td valign="top">Fence is distracting. Nice shot though</td>', 'Fence is distracting. Nice shot though', '2003-11-17 12:49:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(488099, 46235, 13655, '<td valign="top">You should have cropped the US ensign out of the picture.</td>', 'You should have cropped the US ensign out of the picture.', '2003-11-17 13:03:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(488106, 46564, 6999, '<td valign="top">The very low contrast here doesn''t help - it seems to be all midtones, no whites, no blacks. Composition is odd - why crop out the end of the needle? Such very simple subjects almost always rely on great technical work for their impact: try having a careful look at the impact of more directional lighting - this seems to be absolutely flat light - like in an office, or showroom. There''s no shadows at all, no depth, texture.</td>', 'The very low contrast here doesn''t help - it seems to be all midtones, no whites, no blacks. Composition is odd - why crop out the end of the needle? Such very simple subjects almost always rely on great technical work for their impact: try having a careful look at the impact of more directional lighting - this seems to be absolutely flat light - like in an office, or showroom. There''s no shadows at all, no depth, texture.', '2003-11-17 13:07:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(488109, 46649, 6999, '<td valign="top">Very strange that this idea''s cropped up twice - though i think differently done this time.</td>', 'Very strange that this idea''s cropped up twice - though i think differently done this time.', '2003-11-17 13:13:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(488110, 45828, 6999, '<td valign="top">Horriblly unflattering flash-lighting.</td>', 'Horriblly unflattering flash-lighting.', '2003-11-17 13:14:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(488114, 46002, 6999, '<td valign="top">Incredibly sharp image - either a really still night or a fabulous piece of USM work. Star filter, and that''s the moon, yeah? I like the way the extraordinary light in the sky contrasts with the humdrum world below - and the colour in the trees is just enough to add a little visual interest to that humdrum world.</td>', 'Incredibly sharp image - either a really still night or a fabulous piece of USM work. Star filter, and that''s the moon, yeah? I like the way the extraordinary light in the sky contrasts with the humdrum world below - and the colour in the trees is just enough to add a little visual interest to that humdrum world.', '2003-11-17 13:18:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(488134, 46404, 6999, '<td valign="top">Not bad at all - just a couple of problems for me. Firstly the feather seems to be too much shadowed by the ink bottle, and there seems to be a lack of detail in the rendition of it: the image looks as though it has already been sharpened, so maybe the focus isn''t quite there (unless this is a Nikon 5400 shot, in which case it''s just one of those weird ones). The other thing is that the cropping has really crowded the image for me - so close to the edge of the bottle, the feather''s shadow, almost creates a fake tension about whether the subject will actually fit in the image. A little space around things isn''t necessarily ''dead'' space.</td>', 'Not bad at all - just a couple of problems for me. Firstly the feather seems to be too much shadowed by the ink bottle, and there seems to be a lack of detail in the rendition of it: the image looks as though it has already been sharpened, so maybe the focus isn''t quite there (unless this is a Nikon 5400 shot, in which case it''s just one of those weird ones). The other thing is that the cropping has really crowded the image for me - so close to the edge of the bottle, the feather''s shadow, almost creates a fake tension about whether the subject will actually fit in the image. A little space around things isn''t necessarily ''dead'' space.', '2003-11-17 13:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(488136, 45891, 10643, '<td valign="top">I just HAD to look and see if this was a real book title, and I''m glad I did! there''s a whole series! anyway, about the photo, I like it, though if you had control over where the frog was a more interesting wall like brick might have served to provide more interest and contrast. the lighting also seems somewhat harsh; a softer and warmer light instead of a flash would avoid that.</td>', 'I just HAD to look and see if this was a real book title, and I''m glad I did! there''s a whole series! anyway, about the photo, I like it, though if you had control over where the frog was a more interesting wall like brick might have served to provide more interest and contrast. the lighting also seems somewhat harsh; a softer and warmer light instead of a flash would avoid that.', '2003-11-17 13:35:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(488138, 46356, 6999, '<td valign="top">Damn and there actually ARE 39 steps - well done, great care taken. Something not quite satisfying about the image though - perhaps that one set of stairs seems straight, and the other curved, or perhaps the over-lap of the nearer set with the farther tank ... though you''re definitely on the right lines, I think. Exposure''s good, detail''s good - it''s just the composition that needs strengthening, critically in an image that relies almost solely on composition for its effect. Stilll giving you a 7, for gettting close though.</td>', 'Damn and there actually ARE 39 steps - well done, great care taken. Something not quite satisfying about the image though - perhaps that one set of stairs seems straight, and the other curved, or perhaps the over-lap of the nearer set with the farther tank ... though you''re definitely on the right lines, I think. Exposure''s good, detail''s good - it''s just the composition that needs strengthening, critically in an image that relies almost solely on composition for its effect. Stilll giving you a 7, for gettting close though.', '2003-11-17 13:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(488143, 46644, 6999, '<td valign="top">Bloody hell, someone wrote a whole book about Salsa? A WHOLE book? <br/> <br/>Reasonable shot - but overlit, I think: you''ve taken almost all the shadowsing away, and it''s shadowing that gives depth and texture and the third dimension to photography.  There is SOME, of course, but it''s very slight, very (too) subtle. Still, at least you didn;t take it with a full frontal flash. Slightly over-exposed on the garlic and the cloth too - you could have taken at least half a stop off I think. Pretty enough composition, but I find no excitement in it I''m afraid. 6</td>', 'Bloody hell, someone wrote a whole book about Salsa? A WHOLE book?  Reasonable shot - but overlit, I think: you''ve taken almost all the shadowsing away, and it''s shadowing that gives depth and texture and the third dimension to photography.  There is SOME, of course, but it''s very slight, very (too) subtle. Still, at least you didn;t take it with a full frontal flash. Slightly over-exposed on the garlic and the cloth too - you could have taken at least half a stop off I think. Pretty enough composition, but I find no excitement in it I''m afraid. 6', '2003-11-17 13:53:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(488144, 46410, 13384, '<td valign="top">Very inventive and holds well to theme.  Seems to have a deep orange/yellow hue on everything though, I would prefer to have the good crisp chrome reflections and color definition as well as a bit more depth-of-field.</td>', 'Very inventive and holds well to theme.  Seems to have a deep orange/yellow hue on everything though, I would prefer to have the good crisp chrome reflections and color definition as well as a bit more depth-of-field.', '2003-11-17 13:53:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(488147, 46002, 13384, '<td valign="top">Great color and exposure depth, bet you wish you could spot-edit out some of those lens reflections.  Have a bit of trouble connecting the title though...good photo.</td>', 'Great color and exposure depth, bet you wish you could spot-edit out some of those lens reflections.  Have a bit of trouble connecting the title though...good photo.', '2003-11-17 13:56:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(488151, 46666, 13384, '<td valign="top">Love the fact that the BG is not perfect black, it add a mysterious depth to the shot in my view.  The subtle exposure on the head vs the harsh highlights on the eyes and the beak are very nice.  Great shot.</td>', 'Love the fact that the BG is not perfect black, it add a mysterious depth to the shot in my view.  The subtle exposure on the head vs the harsh highlights on the eyes and the beak are very nice.  Great shot.', '2003-11-17 13:58:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(488155, 46320, 12475, '<td valign="top">Great wildlife shot--the turquoise eye is gorgeous.</td>', 'Great wildlife shot--the turquoise eye is gorgeous.', '2003-11-17 14:00:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(488156, 46601, 6999, '<td valign="top">Neat idea, but let down by the poor lighting and the odd composition - why exclude half of the other half of the orange? Just to fit with the ''rule of thirds''? The lighting is far too even to create any sense of plasicity in the subject - appears very flat and pretty boring - would love to see some shading in these oranges ...</td>', 'Neat idea, but let down by the poor lighting and the odd composition - why exclude half of the other half of the orange? Just to fit with the ''rule of thirds''? The lighting is far too even to create any sense of plasicity in the subject - appears very flat and pretty boring - would love to see some shading in these oranges ...', '2003-11-17 14:00:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(488157, 46418, 6999, '<td valign="top">Blunt, ugly, in-your-face and excellent photoraphy. In a sense. Might have been more impact from a beautifully set-up studio shot of the same carcass - the contrast of the perfect/cosmetic studio situation with the toughness of the planet would be arresting.</td>', 'Blunt, ugly, in-your-face and excellent photoraphy. In a sense. Might have been more impact from a beautifully set-up studio shot of the same carcass - the contrast of the perfect/cosmetic studio situation with the toughness of the planet would be arresting.', '2003-11-17 14:05:34.000000', NULL, 1),
