(488944, 46395, 12792, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot of the Bristolian.  I wish the lanterns weren''t burned out, but the range on this shot must have been daunting to capture.  I''d love to see a finished print using a contrast mask to increase and control the apparent range of values.<br/> <br/>Great image but a bit too literal for the theme. <br/></td>', 'Wonderful shot of the Bristolian.  I wish the lanterns weren''t burned out, but the range on this shot must have been daunting to capture.  I''d love to see a finished print using a contrast mask to increase and control the apparent range of values. Great image but a bit too literal for the theme. ', '2003-11-18 15:21:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(488948, 46489, 12792, '<td valign="top">From the literary perspective,  I don''t get it, (though I''m by no means a scholar of British legend). Nice shot of the Canada Goose though!  I love the color family match (Grass to Water) and the color contrast of the goose to them both.  Frankly one of the better pictures I''ve seen of a grounded goose.</td>', 'From the literary perspective,  I don''t get it, (though I''m by no means a scholar of British legend). Nice shot of the Canada Goose though!  I love the color family match (Grass to Water) and the color contrast of the goose to them both.  Frankly one of the better pictures I''ve seen of a grounded goose.', '2003-11-18 15:23:23.000000', NULL, 1),
